  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "Frame stores locals, remaining Body, and result destination; Configuration stores one heap and the frame list. RawStep.store evaluates RHS, obtains Writable and Replaceable in that evaluated state, then Write, and advances only the top statement list. Step.collect collects the raw result once, using rootState's flattened locals of every frame. There is no intermediate collector premise. Raw return/exit retain StoreFinished, and separate class-drop calls and struct-drop steps match the inherited explicit-drop narrative.",
  "limitations": [
    "Statement-level semantic correspondence review; Lean kernel checking of proof terms and mechanical command receipts are separate evidence. This review is not independent of all supporting proof work: the reviewer authored StoreProgress and StoreGarbage."
  ],
